[{"id":61848,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/second-countable.20regular.20spaces.20are.20paracompact/near/61848\">#1</a> I was going to be lazy and follow Akhil Mathew’s proof <a href=\"https://amathew.wordpress.com/2010/08/19/a-theorem-of-michael-on-paracompactness/\">here</a>. But now I see that I don’t follow where he wrote (way back): “I claim that the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_\\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0528em;\">β</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> are locally finite.”</p>","timestamp":1495020513,"subject":"second-countable regular spaces are paracompact","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":61851,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/second-countable.20regular.20spaces.20are.20paracompact/near/61851\">#2</a> In any case, that discussion should be at <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Michael%27s%20theorem\">Michael's theorem</a></em> instead. </p>\n<p>So I have added at <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/second-countable%20regular%20spaces%20are%20paracompact\">second-countable regular spaces are paracompact</a></em> the statement and the easy proof as a corollary of Michael’s theorem.</p>","timestamp":1495025180,"subject":"second-countable regular spaces are paracompact","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":61854,"sender_id":29,"sender_full_name":"Todd_Trimble","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/078428beaeaddf058781b9be6b2c240f?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/second-countable.20regular.20spaces.20are.20paracompact/near/61854\">#3</a> Re <a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/second-countable.20regular.20spaces.20are.20paracompact/near/61848\">#1</a>: this is in the proof of Lemma 3?  Is there a more precise spot in that paragraph that could can point to where you’re stuck?</p>","timestamp":1495027635,"subject":"second-countable regular spaces are paracompact","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":61855,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/second-countable.20regular.20spaces.20are.20paracompact/near/61855\">#4</a> Sorry, yes. At the very end of that paragraph: The <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G_\\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">κ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> are a <em>closed</em> cover. To draw the conclusion at the end of the paragraph, would we not need that their interiors still cover?</p>","timestamp":1495029356,"subject":"second-countable regular spaces are paracompact","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]